      "id": 478763,
      "username": "NeerajL",
      "name": "Neeraj Lilani",
      "created_at": "2025-08-24T16:08:34.959Z",
      "cooked": "<p><strong>Problem Statement</strong>:<br>\nWhen creating a Sales Invoice or Purchase Receipt, there’s no quick view of the item’s last selling/buying price or current cost price. In my trading and wholesale operations, this leads to manual lookups, increasing errors and time, especially for high-volume items.</p>\n<p><strong>Proposed Feature</strong>:<br>\nAutomatically show fields for “Last Selling Price,” “Last Buying Price,” and “Cost Price” (from stock valuation) in the item row of Sales/Purchase forms. Make it visible on item selection, with an option to override or use it for auto-populating rates.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefits/Use Case</strong>:<br>\nImproves pricing accuracy and efficiency—e.g., ensuring we don’t undersell below cost in retail. Useful for finance students/business owners like me analyzing margins on the fly.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/neerajl/{size}/89832_2.png",
